{"duration_api_ms":315068,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"bd9f8775-e937-4927-97fd-e02a18073361","total_cost_usd":0.359958,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12836,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":30861,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":24259},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12836,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":30861,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12836,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12836},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":30861,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12836,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.359958,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":24259,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"None of the 20 evaluated designs is feasible: 11 returned no geometry and the 9 that ran each violate at least one constraint. The constraint limits back-computed from the margins are max_g <= 12, bondline temperature <= 450 K and bluntness <= 1.2. The heatshield mass limit is not stated. Geometry failures come from a small cone angle combined with high bluntness or large diameter. A rough fit to the reported negative cone lengths gives a validity condition of about 0.917*b*cos(theta) + 0.133*(1-cos(theta)) < 0.5, checked by hand against the data. I keep it below about 0.46. The mass-fraction ratio scales roughly with D^2 and falls with cone angle, about 0.087*D^2 relative to the limit at 70 deg. A diameter of about 3.0-3.3 m with high cone angle should therefore sit near the mass limit. Peak g is set mainly by |gamma|: about 11.4 at 3.08 deg, 11.9 at 3.5 deg and 12.7 at 3.96 deg, so |gamma| must stay at or below roughly 3.5 deg. Peak heat flux fits q ~ 295e3*sqrt((m/A)*sin|gamma|/(b*D)) to within about 5-10%, and bondline temperature rise fits roughly 14*Y^0.4*sin|gamma|^-0.3 with Y = sqrt((m/A)/(b*D*sin|gamma|)). Both fits are my own regressions on 9 points. So the region to target is D about 2.7-3.3 m, b about 1.0-1.18, theta 66-70 deg and |gamma| about 2-3.6 deg.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-1b6a532a4589: margin_g 0.00983 at 11.882 g gives limit 12; T 456.89 at margin -0.01531 gives limit 450; C-763297ba691c: b 1.2307 at margin -0.02558 gives limit 1.2.\",\"Invalid geometries: C-ef541f66418a (b 1.18, theta 61.9), C-68844c149dc6 (b 0.99, theta 59.7, D 2.0) and C-8918773e968b (b 0.87, theta 52.7, D 4.05). Valid: C-763297ba691c (b 1.23, theta 69.8), C-7929904365f5 and C-0f5c4bbcbbf2. High bluntness needs theta near 70 deg.\",\"Mass fraction: C-763297ba691c (D 2.5, margin +0.45), C-7929904365f5 (D 3.63, -0.18), C-d0ebb2a4a17d (D 4.3, -0.69), C-a7c3287a38ba (D 4.36, -0.99). Low-theta rows C-04af890b3186 (theta 31, -0.52) and C-697f9dd9337a (theta 38, +0.08) show higher mass per D^2.\",\"g vs gamma: C-d0ebb2a4a17d gamma -3.08 gives 11.45 g, C-1b6a532a4589 gamma -3.50 gives 11.88 g, C-7929904365f5 gamma -3.96 gives 12.71 g, C-951f544259a7 gamma -5.09 gives 14.58 g.\",\"Heat flux scaling holds across rows: C-763297ba691c 447k, C-d0ebb2a4a17d 333k, C-7929904365f5 320k, C-697f9dd9337a 668k, C-1b6a532a4589 1.07M. The fitted constant is 280-308k.\",\"Bondline T rises as gamma gets shallower and diameter smaller: C-1b6a532a4589 (D 1.65) 457 K, C-d0ebb2a4a17d 404 K, C-0f5c4bbcbbf2 (steep, D 3.86) 367 K.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Ballistic-entry scaling from prior knowledge, checked against the rows above. Peak stagnation heat flux scales with sqrt(ballistic coefficient * sin gamma / nose radius). Bondline temperature follows the integrated heat load, which grows with a low-drag, small-nose-radius, shallow-entry pulse. A larger diameter lowers the ballistic coefficient and so lowers both objectives, but it is capped by heatshield mass fraction. A larger bluntness raises the nose radius and lowers heat flux, but it is capped at 1.2 and by geometry validity, which needs a large cone half-angle. Steeper entry lowers bondline temperature but raises g, which is capped at 12. Because the reference is 450 K over a 150 K range, bondline temperature dominates the hypervolume. The best feasible region should therefore be the corner of maximum diameter, maximum bluntness, theta about 70 deg and |gamma| near the g limit.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The geometry-validity fit, mass-fraction scaling and g(gamma) relation are inferred from 9 valid points and can be off by a few percent. Diameters of 3.3-3.4 m sit at the mass boundary, and |gamma| of 3.5-3.6 deg sits at the g boundary. Whether high bluntness and cone angle lower g at a given gamma is unknown. The bondline-temperature fit has about 5-10 K scatter. Low-gamma probes (2-2.4 deg) risk unmodelled skip-out or long-pulse effects.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-763297ba691c\",\"rationale\":\"Core candidate: bluntness just under the 1.2 limit, theta 70 deg for validity and low mass, D 3.0 m, gamma -3.4 deg for g of about 11.8.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.18,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":269000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"First likely-feasible point; anchors the fitted heat-flux, bondline-temperature and mass models.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-763297ba691c\",\"rationale\":\"Larger D lowers ballistic coefficient; predicted mass fraction about 0.90 of the limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.18,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":240000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the mass-fraction constraint near its expected boundary with lower predicted objectives.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-763297ba691c\",\"rationale\":\"Push D to 3.3 m; predicted mass fraction about 0.96 of the limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.18,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":229000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the mass-fraction boundary; a pass gives a strong corner point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7929904365f5\",\"rationale\":\"Deliberate boundary probe: D 3.4 m at theta 70 deg is predicted just over the mass limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.4,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.18,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":223000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.0,\"feasible\":false},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Brackets the maximum usable diameter for the final round; a pass would move the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-763297ba691c\",\"rationale\":\"Smaller D leaves mass margin for a steeper gamma of -3.45 deg.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.8,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.18,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":300000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Mass-safe fallback point that also tests g near 11.85.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-763297ba691c\",\"rationale\":\"D 2.7 m hedges against the mass-fraction estimate being optimistic.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.7,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.18,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":315000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":405.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Safe feasible design near the boundary; sensitivity to D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7929904365f5\",\"rationale\":\"Lower bluntness (1.0) with theta 66 deg tests the bluntness effect on heat flux at fixed D and gamma.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":292000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether the sqrt(1/(b*D)) scaling holds and whether theta 66 stays valid.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-763297ba691c\",\"rationale\":\"Shallower gamma of -2.8 deg trades higher bondline T for lower heat flux and lower g.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.18,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":244000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":408.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Maps the trade-off front in gamma at fixed geometry.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-d0ebb2a4a17d\",\"rationale\":\"Gamma -2.4 deg extends the front toward low heat flux.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.18,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":226000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Covers the low-heat-flux end of the trade-off and tests the bondline temperature extrapolation.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-d0ebb2a4a17d\",\"rationale\":\"Gamma -2.0 deg is the low-flux extreme; bondline T should stay under 450 K.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.18,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":206000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":428.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the front and tests extrapolation to very shallow entry, where heat load and any skip-out behaviour are unmodelled.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-763297ba691c\",\"rationale\":\"Large D at shallower gamma of -2.8 deg to see combined effects.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.18,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":211000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Low heat flux with lower g margin risk; a second point on the large-D branch.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7929904365f5\",\"rationale\":\"Gamma -3.6 deg tests whether high bluntness and theta let g stay at or below 12.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.18,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":276000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.7,\"feasible\":false},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the g boundary; g is predicted at about 12.0-12.1 by interpolation of the nearby rows.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-763297ba691c\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.2 m with gamma -3.55 deg pushes toward the g and mass boundaries together.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.18,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":249000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"A pass gives the best predicted bondline temperature among the plausible feasible designs.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7929904365f5\",\"rationale\":\"Moderate bluntness 0.8 with theta 60 deg and D 3.2 m tests a different cone angle and nose radius.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.8,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":60.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":292000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":404.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the theta-dependent mass fraction and geometry validity at theta 60.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-951f544259a7\",\"rationale\":\"Intermediate design: D 3.1 m, b 0.9, theta 66 deg, gamma -3.3 deg.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.9,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":288500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":403.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds a mid-bluntness point to separate the effects of bluntness and diameter.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1b6a532a4589\",\"rationale\":\"D 2.9 m, b 1.1, theta 68 deg, gamma -3.5 deg gives a mass-safe design at the g edge.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.9,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":297000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests validity at theta 68 deg with b 1.1, and g at 3.5 deg.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-763297ba691c\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-range gamma of -3.0 deg with D 3.15 m and b 1.15.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.15,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":237600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the front between the gamma -2.8 and -3.3 deg points.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-763297ba691c\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.25 m, b 1.1, gamma -3.1 deg as another mass-boundary sample.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":235700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extra data on mass and bondline temperature at high D with slightly lower bluntness.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-d0ebb2a4a17d\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.3 m with lower bluntness of 1.0 separates the bluntness effect from the diameter effect at the mass boundary.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":245000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether mass fraction depends on bluntness at high D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-763297ba691c\",\"rationale\":\"Fill point at gamma -3.0 deg with D 3.0 m and b 1.18.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.18,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":252000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":404.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Gives a smooth gamma sweep at fixed geometry for a clean model of the trade-off.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":260651,"type":"result","duration_ms":315109,"uuid":"62f5620c-4052-4e6f-8384-44e7c31e6aae","ttft_stream_ms":1627,"time_to_request_ms":53,"first_content_frame_ms":1628,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
